<%# Meal pog guidelines — ported from port/components/hq-pog-guidelines.hbs with
    the ReadMore expanders rebuilt on the existing read-more Stimulus pattern.
    Rendered inside the pog issue dialog for meal-type pogs only (suppressed for
    shower pogs, as upstream). Each row comes from the pog_guideline partial,
    which wires its id to the toggle's aria-controls. %>
Meal pog guidelines:
<div class="my-2 mx-3">
  <%= render layout: "hq/shift_manage/pog_guideline",
             locals: { icon: "utensils", id: "hq-pog-guideline-1",
                       heading: "One pog for 6+ hours, two for 10+ hours — for one of " \
                                "the next three meals, not 24-hour period" } do %>
    Issue a pog only for one of the three meals after the shift ends &mdash; not for a
    24-hour window. Example: a shift ending at 18:15 earns a pog for that night&rsquo;s
    dinner, or the next day&rsquo;s breakfast or lunch. Two pogs may cover two different
    meals in that window.
  <% end %>

  <%= render layout: "hq/shift_manage/pog_guideline",
             locals: { icon: "ban", id: "hq-pog-guideline-2", emphasis: "text-error",
                       heading: "No pog for a shift under 6 hours — unless they rangered " \
                                "two back-to-back shifts totaling 6+ hours" } do %>
    <p class="mb-2">
      Two back-to-back shifts totaling over 6 hours are eligible for one pog. Example: a
      Burn Perimeter shift followed straight by a Dirt shift earns one pog for the 6+
      combined hours, not one per shift.
    </p>
    If the combined time exceeds 10 hours, issue two pogs.
  <% end %>

  <%= render layout: "hq/shift_manage/pog_guideline",
             locals: { icon: "people-group", id: "hq-pog-guideline-3",
                       heading: "Mentors, Sandman, and Gerlach Patrol handle their own " \
                                "— no pogs issued" } do %>
    <p class="mb-2">
      Mentors and Sandman receive pogs directly from their Cadres. Gerlach Patrol gets to
      eat at Bruno&rsquo;s for free.
    </p>
    A Ranger may walk up to the HQ Window and claim they were approved for a pog. The HQ Lead
    must confirm that authorization with the right Cadre before you issue it.
  <% end %>

  <%= render layout: "hq/shift_manage/pog_guideline",
             locals: { icon: "shuffle", id: "hq-pog-guideline-4",
                       heading: "Pog swaps — only for the same three-meal window and " \
                                "only one swap allowed" } do %>
    <p class="mb-2">
      You may swap a pog for a different meal. The new meal must fall inside the original
      three-meal window after the shift ended &mdash; not inside a 24-hour period.
    </p>
    Count from the shift, not from when the Ranger returns to ask. Grant only one
    replacement pog per shift.
  <% end %>

  <%= render layout: "hq/shift_manage/pog_guideline",
             locals: { icon: "person-walking-arrow-loop-left", id: "hq-pog-guideline-5",
                       heading: "Forgotten Pog — only for the three-meal window after " \
                                "the shift" } do %>
    <p class="mb-2">
      You may issue a pog later. It still has to fall inside the three-meal window after
      the shift ended &mdash; count from the shift, not from when the Ranger comes back
      to ask.
    </p>
    The Ranger, not HQ, is responsible for getting a pog.
  <% end %>

  <%= render layout: "hq/shift_manage/pog_guideline",
             locals: { icon: "question", id: "hq-pog-guideline-6",
                       heading: "Questions and Exceptions" } do %>
    <p class="mb-2">
      For questions, talk with the HQ Short or HQ Lead. For exceptions, refer the person to
      the HQ Lead.
    </p>
    <em>Ranger Commissary Meals Policy</em> sets the pog rules. Find it in the
    <em>Ranger Department Policies, Protocols, and Procedures</em> folder on Google Drive.
    The Clubhouse Homepage links to the Ranger Google Drive in its
    <em>Links &amp; Things</em> section.
  <% end %>
</div>
